{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/physical-chemical-changes/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/physical-chemical-changes.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Physical & Chemical Changes | Chemistry Foundations","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations\n      </a>\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-rose-400 to-pink-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -sync-alt text-rose-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"sync\">sync</span>Physical &amp; Chemical Changes\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding the differences between changes that affect physical form versus chemical identity.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-rose-50 border-l-4 border-rose-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-rose-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Distinguish between physical and chemical changes</li>\n          <li>• Identify evidence of chemical changes</li>\n          <li>• Give examples of each type of change</li>\n          <li>• Understand reversible and irreversible changes</li>\n          <li>• Apply knowledge to classify everyday changes</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: Physical Changes -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          Physical Changes\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-100 to-cyan-100 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-1\">Definition</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">physical change</strong> is a change in which no new substance is formed. The substance only changes its physical state, shape, or size.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -cube mr-2\" data-mi=\"view_in_ar\">view_in_ar</span>Characteristics</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• No new substance formed</li>\n                <li>• Easily reversible</li>\n                <li>• No change in chemical composition</li>\n                <li>• Usually no heat/light produced</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -list mr-2\" data-mi=\"list\">list</span>Examples</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Melting ice → water</li>\n                <li>• Boiling water → steam</li>\n                <li>• Dissolving salt in water</li>\n                <li>• Crushing a can</li>\n                <li>• Tearing paper</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Key Point</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">In physical changes, the same substance is present before and after the change. Water is still H₂O whether it's ice, liquid, or steam!</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Chemical Changes -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Chemical Changes\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-100 to-red-100 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-1\">Definition</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A <strong class=\"text-orange-600\">chemical change</strong> (chemical reaction) is a change in which one or more new substances are formed with different properties from the original substances.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -atom mr-2\" data-mi=\"atom\">atom</span>Characteristics</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• New substance(s) formed</li>\n                <li>• Usually difficult to reverse</li>\n                <li>• Change in chemical composition</li>\n                <li>• Often involves heat, light, or gas</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -fire mr-2\" data-mi=\"local_fire_department\">local_fire_department</span>Examples</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Burning wood → ash + gases</li>\n                <li>• Rusting iron → iron oxide</li>\n                <li>• Cooking an egg</li>\n                <li>• Baking a cake</li>\n                <li>• Souring milk</li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Evidence of Chemical Change -->\n        <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-orange-200\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -search mr-2\" data-mi=\"search\">search</span>Evidence of Chemical Change:</h4>\n          <div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded text-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -fire text-orange-500 text-2xl mb-1\" data-mi=\"local_fire_department\">local_fire_department</span>\n              <p class=\"text-sm font-medium\">Heat/Light</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">produced</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded text-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -wind text-blue-500 text-2xl mb-1\" data-mi=\"air\">air</span>\n              <p class=\"text-sm font-medium\">Gas</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">bubbles formed</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded text-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -palette text-purple-500 text-2xl mb-1\" data-mi=\"palette\">palette</span>\n              <p class=\"text-sm font-medium\">Color Change</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">unexpected</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-3 rounded text-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -cloud text-gray-500 text-2xl mb-1\" data-mi=\"cloud\">cloud</span>\n              <p class=\"text-sm font-medium\">Precipitate</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500\">solid forms</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Comparison Table -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Physical vs Chemical Changes\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-gray-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <thead class=\"bg-rose-600 text-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-left\">Aspect</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Physical Change</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Chemical Change</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">New substance</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-blue-600\">No</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-orange-600\">Yes</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Reversibility</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-blue-600\">Usually easy</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-orange-600\">Usually difficult</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Chemical composition</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-blue-600\">Unchanged</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-orange-600\">Changed</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Energy changes</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-blue-600\">Minimal</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-orange-600\">Often significant</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Examples</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-blue-600\">Melting, dissolving</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center text-orange-600\">Burning, rusting</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Common Examples -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Classifying Common Changes\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Physical Changes</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-blue-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Melting candle wax</strong> - wax changes from solid to liquid</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-blue-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Dissolving sugar in tea</strong> - sugar disperses but remains sugar</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-blue-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Breaking glass</strong> - smaller pieces, still glass</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-blue-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Freezing water</strong> - liquid becomes solid ice</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-blue-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Magnetizing iron</strong> - magnetic property added</span>\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"bg-orange-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-orange-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -times-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"cancel\">cancel</span>Chemical Changes</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-orange-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Burning candle wax</strong> - wax reacts with oxygen → CO₂ + H₂O</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-orange-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Baking bread</strong> - yeast fermentation produces gas</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-orange-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Rusting iron</strong> - Fe + O₂ + H₂O → Fe₂O₃ (rust)</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-orange-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Cooking egg</strong> - proteins denature, texture changes</span>\n              </li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\">\n                <span class=\"text-orange-500 mt-0.5\">•</span>\n                <span><strong>Burning paper</strong> - paper → ash + gases</span>\n              </li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Tricky Cases -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-rose-100 text-rose-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Tricky Cases Explained\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-gray-50 text-left font-semibold text-gray-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-gray-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -question-circle mr-2 text-gray-500\" data-mi=\"help\">help</span>Dissolving: Physical or Chemical?</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700\">Dissolving is generally a <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">physical change</strong>. The solute (like salt) spreads throughout the solvent (water) but no new substance forms. The salt can be recovered by evaporation.</p>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700 mt-2\">However, dissolving some substances like sodium metal in water IS chemical because hydrogen gas and sodium hydroxide are produced!</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-orange-50 text-left font-semibold text-orange-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-orange-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -question-circle mr-2 text-orange-500\" data-mi=\"help\">help</span>Is boiling water a chemical change?</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <p class=\"text-gray-700\"><strong class=\"text-blue-600\">No, it's physical!</strong> Boiling water turns liquid H₂O into gaseous H₂O (steam). No new substance forms - it's still water, just in gas form. The steam can condense back to liquid water.</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-blue-50 text-left font-semibold text-blue-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-blue-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -question-circle mr-2 text-blue-500\" data-mi=\"help\">help</span>Why is a burning candle both physical and chemical?</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n                  <li><strong class=\"text-blue-600\">Physical part:</strong> The solid wax melts (state change)</li>\n                  <li><strong class=\"text-orange-600\">Chemical part:</strong> The wax vapor burns with oxygen to form CO₂ and H₂O (new substances)</li>\n                </ul>\n                <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-2\">The melting is reversible, but the burning is not.</p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-rose-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Classify as physical or chemical: (a) Melting ice, (b) Burning wood, (c) Dissolving salt in water, (d) Rusting nail</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>(a) Melting ice - <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">Physical</strong> (state change)</p>\n                <p>(b) Burning wood - <strong class=\"text-orange-600\">Chemical</strong> (new substances: ash, CO₂)</p>\n                <p>(c) Dissolving salt - <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">Physical</strong> (no new substance)</p>\n                <p>(d) Rusting nail - <strong class=\"text-orange-600\">Chemical</strong> (iron oxide forms)</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Give three pieces of evidence that a chemical change has occurred.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Any three of:</p>\n                <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside mt-1\">\n                  <li>Color change (unexpected)</li>\n                  <li>Gas produced (bubbles)</li>\n                  <li>Heat or light produced</li>\n                  <li>Precipitate formed</li>\n                  <li>Difficult to reverse</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Explain why cooking an egg is a chemical change.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Cooking an egg is chemical because:</p>\n                <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside mt-1\">\n                  <li>The proteins in the egg denature and re-form new structures</li>\n                  <li>The texture, color, and taste change permanently</li>\n                  <li>It cannot be reversed - you can't un-cook an egg!</li>\n                  <li>New substances with different properties are formed</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. Is boiling an egg physical or chemical? Explain.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Boiling an egg is a <strong class=\"text-orange-600\">chemical change</strong>. While the boiling water is physical, the egg itself undergoes chemical changes - the proteins denature and the egg becomes solid. This is irreversible.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-rose-50 to-pink-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-rose-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-rose-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways for WAEC/JAMB/NECO</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-rose-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• <strong>Physical:</strong> No new substance, reversible, state/shape changes only</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Chemical:</strong> New substance(s) formed, usually irreversible</li>\n            <li>• Evidence of chemical change: color, gas, heat/light, precipitate</li>\n            <li>• Dissolving is usually physical (but check for reactions)</li>\n            <li>• State changes (melting, boiling) are always physical</li>\n            <li>• Burning is always chemical (combustion)</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-rose-50 to-pink-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card { transition: all 0.2s ease; }\n    .step-card:hover { transform: translateX(4px); }\n    #topic-complete-btn { transition: all 0.3s ease; }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover { transform: scale(1.02); }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"physical-chemical-changes","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"Which is a physical change?","options":["Burning paper","Rusting iron","Melting ice","Cooking egg"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Melting ice is a physical change - only the state changes from solid to liquid. No new substance forms."},{"question":"Which indicates a chemical change?","options":["Change of shape","Change of state","Color change with new substance","Change of size"],"correct":2,"explanation":"An unexpected color change that produces a new substance indicates a chemical reaction."},{"question":"Dissolving sugar in water is:","options":["Chemical change","Physical change","Both","Neither"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Dissolving sugar is physical - no new substance forms. Sugar can be recovered by evaporation."},{"question":"Which is evidence of a chemical reaction?","options":["Melting","Freezing","Gas bubbles forming","Dissolving"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Gas bubbles (effervescence) indicate a new gas is being produced - a sign of chemical change."},{"question":"Rusting of iron is a:","options":["Physical change","Chemical change","Reversible change","Temporary change"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Rusting is chemical - iron reacts with oxygen and water to form iron oxide (rust), a new substance."},{"question":"Which is reversible?","options":["Burning wood","Baking cake","Melting wax","Cooking meat"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Melting wax is reversible - the wax can solidify again. The others are permanent chemical changes."},{"question":"Boiling water is a physical change because:","options":["Bubbles are formed","Heat is needed","No new substance forms","Steam escapes"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Boiling water is physical because H₂O remains H₂O - only the state changes from liquid to gas."},{"question":"Which change produces heat and light?","options":["Melting ice","Burning candle","Dissolving salt","Freezing water"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Burning (combustion) produces heat and light - it's always a chemical change."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"physical-chemical-changes","topicTitle":"Physical & Chemical Changes","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}